"""Human-authored final wording for individually adjudicated claims. No inferred verdicts."""
def polish(C,I,R):
    # The indexed item statements are already carefully scoped prose. Reuse them explicitly
    # for the parallel claim while retaining separate fate, proof and literature fields.
    for c in C:
        n=int(c['id'].rsplit('-',1)[1])-16000
        if n<=86:
            c['his_statement']=I[n]['his_words']
            c['statement']=I[n]['statement']
    wording={
    1:('Asserted without an integral qualification.','The exact exterior-algebra computation gives ξ^n=n!vol. In rank4 the top map has cokernel Z/2.','The literal assertion is false. The rational replacement is standard; no later publication of this exact erroneous integral statement was located.','False over Z; the factorial obstruction disappears over Q.'),
    2:('The normalization is implicit; formula(6.5) is blank.','Raw contraction gives Λ0L0(1)=n, while unit lowering gives ΛL(1)=1. The script verifies both for n=1,…,5.','The two normalizations are distinct. The later rational sl2 literature does not identify their integral orders.','Retain the normalization distinction and the blank formula.'),
    3:('The author already answers negatively.','Conjugation by1+tL fixes L and changes Λ to Λ+t(π2−π0)−t²L. This is an independent matrix proof.','The source’s negative answer is correct. No separate publication of this exact integral formulation was located.','L alone does not determine the grading or lowering operator.'),
    4:('Asserted in the reused Brauer text.','Replacing x by x+Qz changes xᵀQ⁻¹y by an integer. The computed determinant3 example and inverse matrix verify the formula.','Published in BrauerIII§8.4. The geometric identification of NS with the discriminant group has additional hypotheses.','The lattice statement is valid.'),
    5:('Resolution independence is asserted without the lattice calculation.','The symbolic congruence SᵀQ′S=Q⊕[−1], with detS=1, proves invariance under one point blowup.','BrauerIII repeats the assertion. Passing between resolutions also uses a common resolution and surface factorization.','The local calculation is complete; the geometric factorization input is explicit.'),
    6:('An unqualified selection step occurs in a reused proof.','All eight elements of F2³ were tested: each generates a subalgebra of size2 or4, never8.','The finite-field argument is false as written. This does not refute standard étale presentations after suitable localization.','Add the appropriate field hypothesis or replace the argument.'),
    8:('Derived from the Kummer sequence on the pages.','Pass to the inverse limit under the stated finiteness and divisibility conditions; TℓBr′ is torsion free. No splitting is inferred.','Published in BrauerIII§8.2. Stacks03PK verifies the finite Kummer input.','The exact sequence is valid with ℓ invertible and the stated Picard/cohomology conditions.'),
    9:('Reused English text explicitly cites Matlis.','Matched Matlis Theorem2.5, Proposition3.1 and Theorems3.9–3.10, including their noetherian hypotheses.','Established by Matlis in1958. The surviving reused leaf has not been attributed to Grothendieck.','Known module theorem; authorship and mathematical validity are separate.'),
    10:('Asserted in the reused injective-sheaf text.','The right adjoint of the exact stalk functor sends an injective hull to an injective sheaf. Matlis decomposition then applies in the noetherian setting.','The qualified statement is standard. The exact publication provenance of this English leaf was not identified.','No general claim that arbitrary pushforward preserves injectives is made.'),
    11:('The leaf starts after missing antecedents.','The opened published §8.4 supplies completeness, normality, dimension2, algebraically closed residue field, coefficient field and regular resolution.','The geometric statement is published under these hypotheses. The coefficient-field assumption excludes an unqualified mixed-characteristic reading.','Use the complete published hypotheses, clearly labelled as recovered context.'),
    12:('The pairing compatibility is not proved on the surviving pages.','The discriminant pairing and local cup-product pairing were separately identified. The comparison map and its conventions were not proved.','Published Remark8.5 expressly says that the verification was not performed. No exact later proof matching these conventions was found in the recorded searches.','This dossier retains a proof obligation; it does not assert that the modern theorem is unknown everywhere.'),
    14:('Definition and properties in a reused étale typescript.','The module is Ω¹B/A over B, so its Fitting presentation must use free B-modules. The historical first ideal corresponds to modern Fitt0.','The corrected mathematical construction matches Stacks49.7. The typed A and Filting spelling remain in the reading record.','Valid after the explicitly editorial module-ring correction.'),
    15:('Transitivity is discussed in a reused different calculation.','The triangular monic tower has Jacobian determinant f_xg_y. This checks the complete-intersection example, not all finite algebra towers.','Modern Kähler, Dedekind and dualizing differents must be distinguished. Unrestricted equality was not verified.','Keep the general inclusion and the stronger qualified equality separate.'),
    16:('Comparison with the Dedekind different.','A purely inseparable field extension has a degenerate trace pairing, showing why generic separability cannot be omitted.','The exact defining hypotheses were read in Stacks49.8–49.9. Classical finite flat complete-intersection/DVR comparisons apply.','Do not apply the trace-inverse description to an arbitrary finite algebra.'),
    17:('Categorical lifting statement in the reused text.','Stacks58.8.3 gives an equivalence of finite étale categories across a thickening, including morphisms.','Established in the étale theory developed in EGA/SGA; exact galley pagination was not identified.','The category equivalence, not merely isomorphism-class lifting, is the proper statement.'),
    18:('The proposition includes two distinct boundedness alternatives.','Over a field, complexes with one copy of k in every nonnegative degree have H0RHom=∏k. Thus both arguments bounded below alone is insufficient.','Stacks36.11.5 verifies opposite boundedness, and47.15.2 verifies the finite-injective-dimension mechanism.','The actual qualified source proposition survives the counterexample to its weakened reading.'),
    20:('An editorial instruction proposes deleting part(ii).','No clause-level comparison was completed: the published49.9MB EGA PDF was blocked by the reader size limit.','EGAIV4 metadata is verified; the proposed18.11.6 match remains unverified.','A deletion request does not establish that a mathematical clause is false.'),
    21:('Reused group-scheme errata, with old galley page references.','The modern root/group-scheme comparators were read, but the precise XV–XVII galley correspondence was not recovered.','No exact published errata match was found. The visible claims lack enough antecedents for a unique modern formulation.','Retain the provenance and pagination uncertainty.'),
    22:('Étale criteria are stated with hypotheses in a reused typescript.','Spec k→Spec(k[ε]/ε²) has finite fibres but is not flat. This isolates the missing premise in an overstrong reading.','Standard étale results require flatness and finite presentation; no unrestricted finite-fibre criterion is valid.','The finite-fibre-only converse is false.'),
    24:('Draft letters and subscripts are partly ambiguous.','Compared the actual published A/B definitions and the supplied second-pass readings. The CSG transcription uses the same scans and is not independent evidence.','Draft C matches published B; draft A matches published A. A full B/D dictionary and the ℓ|χ subscript were not established.','Retain the partial dictionary and literal dates.'),
    26:('An integral normalized operator model is asserted.','For n=1,…,5 every matrix-unit product and endpoint identity was checked; ranks are5,14,30,55,91. The general proof is the block matrix-unit construction.','The conditional algebra is correct. No exact later publication of this integral formulation was located.','Do not identify it with the failed exterior-contraction order over Z.'),
    27:('Second pass confirms the written range2n−i.','A primitive string has positions0,…,n−i. Larger indices give zero vectors, hence cannot index nonzero matrix units.','The range error is certified mathematically; it has not been reclassified as an ink misreading.','The proposed range n−i is an editorial correction.'),
    29:('The source prescribes L and every π_i.','Primitive strings construct the lowering operator and matrix units. Their uniqueness uses the prescribed grading and two-sided inverses.','The conditional ring argument is valid; no exact independent integral publication was identified.','Removing all π_i gives the different, false uniqueness question of claim16003.'),
    30:('A standard conjecture, not a proved inverse theorem.','Deligne provides cohomological hard Lefschetz. Neither it nor Jannsen’s numerical theorem constructs an algebraic lowering correspondence.','The Lefschetz standard conjecture remains unresolved in general. Verified2025 work adds special cases under precise fibration hypotheses.','Known cases include abelian varieties and surfaces; no general solution is claimed.'),
    31:('Live endpoint formulas coexist with cancelled earlier formulas.','On a string v0,…,vm, unit lowering sends vj to vj−1 for j>0. Direct matrix checks verify the endpoint complements.','Kleiman uses the same normalized formalism. Weighted sl2 lowering has different coefficients.','The unit-step identities are valid.'),
    32:('Conditional hyperplane induction and mixed-product criterion.','The string computations verify ΛY=restriction·ΛX²·Gysin; the evanescent middle summand is killed. All critical-degree hypotheses are retained.','The standard formalism supports the qualified induction. The implication B(X)⇒B(Y) does not become an equivalence without the mixed condition.','Do not omit B(Y), smoothness, polarization or the critical-degree restriction.'),
    33:('Weak variants with inconsistent degree notation.','A degree audit identifies the problem but does not determine which visible index was intended.','Related published A/B implications are verified; the exact A′/A″ formulation is not identifiable uniquely.','Reconstruct a precise statement before attempting its proof.'),
    34:('A proof is supplied, with a u/w polynomial slip.','Cayley–Hamilton expresses w⁻¹ as a rational polynomial when its characteristic coefficients are rational and constant coefficient nonzero. The exampleW=[[2,1],[1,1]] has inverse3I−W.','Kleiman2.9–2.10 publishes the qualified criterion and polarization independence.','Rationality is a genuine premise; uniformity across cohomology theories does not follow.'),
    35:('An earlier assertion is expressly retracted and later repaired conditionally.','Both letter layers were read; the literal6.1.1966 date remains unchanged.','The qualified polarization criterion is published. The stronger unconditional realization-independence claim is not established.','Keep the retraction and repair separate.'),
    36:('Semisimplicity is proposed under Lefschetz and index assumptions.','The involution preserves the radical; xx* is nilpotent there, so its trace is zero. Positive definiteness forces x=0. Finite dimension over Q is required.','Kleiman3.11–3.13 proves the conditional result.','This does not establish general homological semisimplicity.'),
    37:('An algebraic splitting is requested under a positivity hypothesis.','The positive adjoint makes u*u invertible; its rational polynomial inverse gives an algebraic left inverse.','Kleiman Corollary3.14 proves the qualified assertion.','Linear injectivity alone does not supply an algebraic correspondence.'),
    38:('A later-run comparison, not an author claim.','Read the equivalence relation in Jannsen’s Theorem1 and the nilpotent-kernel qualification in Corollary1.','Jannsen proves semisimplicity for numerical motives with characteristic-zero coefficients.','The homological category and conjecture B are not thereby settled.'),
    39:('An editorial logical test.','The nonzero ideal(ε) inQ[ε]/ε² is nilpotent. Jannsen’s nilpotent-kernel conclusion therefore cannot mean that the kernel vanishes.','The distinction is elementary and remains material in the motivic comparison.','Nilpotence is not positivity or faithfulness.'),
    40:('A later literature comparison.','Katz–Messing Theorem2 constructs degree projectors by rational polynomial interpolation in Frobenius; its finite-field hypotheses were checked.','The Künneth projectors are algebraic in that setting.','This is weaker than an algebraic Lefschetz inverse.'),
    41:('A dated list of known cases, followed by an expressly rejected reduction.','Second pass reads allπ_i for a surface. The hypersurface reduction imposes a fundamental-group obstruction in the intended smooth characteristic-zero setting.','The known cases agree with the later standard-conjecture exposition. The singular-hypersurface replacement is only a programme.','Do not turn the old list into a current upper bound on knowledge.'),
    42:('A historical attribution reported by Tate.','Located exact title, journal, year and pages. The publisher full text could not be read.','The bibliographic identity is supported by metadata; the full theorem and historical reception claim remain unverified.','Do not present a proof or priority audit as completed.'),
    44:('A theorem with a derived projection/base-change proof sketch.','The biextension identity for Poincaré, derived base change, projection formula and relative Künneth identify convolution with tensor.','Mukai and Laumon establish precise forms; Stacks verifies the chosen perfect-complex preservation criterion.','The category and base hypotheses matter.'),
    45:('An unproved margin generalization.','The pull–tensor–push diagram works with compatible kernels, proper support and suitable Tor conditions. Associativity and unit coherence remain additional checks.','Modern Fourier–Mukai theory supplies variants, but the exact three-torsor statement is not fully formulated on the page.','Retain this as a qualified reconstruction, not a universal theorem.'),
    46:('The theorem is corrected; an obsolete identity target survives in its proof.','The character indexed by a+a′ is trivial on the antidiagonal a′=−a, forcing inversion.','Mukai proves the field equivalence and Laumon the precise relative determinant formula.','The corrected antidiagonal theorem is valid.'),
    47:('Relative determinant and shift factors are displayed.','The derived shift supplies parity on K0, and the determinant line is compared with the dual Hodge bundle without choosing a trivialization.','Laumon1.2.4–1.2.5 and Moonen2.3 retain the required factor.','An invertible line over a field is not thereby canonically trivialized.'),
    48:('The K0 line omits a factor present on the next derived page.','Apply[K[−g]]=(−1)^g[K] and the tensor line class to the derived formula.','The qualified relative formula includes[τ_A].','The shorter formula requires[τ_A]=1.'),
    49:('The proof is cancelled and the lemma admitted.','Checked the field vanishing input in the opened Mukai and Laumon arguments; no independent inspection of Mumford’s full book proof is claimed.','The vanishing is a known abelian-variety theorem.','Do not replace it by an arbitrary relative vanishing assertion.'),
    50:('The author expressly leaves a compatibility verification.','A perfect-cone argument reduces to derived fibres, but matching dimensions and Koszul cohomology objects does not verify the actual comparison map.','Mukai proves the field inversion theorem, and Laumon states the exact relative kernel theorem with its determinant line and shift. The opened Laumon passage recalls the canonical morphism construction but does not write the requested unit-fibre compatibility computation; it is not a second archival proof witness.','The kernel theorem is established in the later literature; this dossier does not claim to have filled the manuscript’s particular morphism-level proof gap.'),
    51:('An earlier-run local reconstruction.','The Koszul resolution yields Λ^(g−i)T∨⊗detT≅Λ^iT; binomial dimensions were checked for g=1,…,6.','This standard calculation agrees with the later kernel theorem.','It identifies objects, not the particular comparison morphism.'),
    52:('A display omits the zero-section pushforward.','The expression must beLψ*(e_*τ[−g]); flatψ removes derived Tor and gives the ordinary zero-fibre sheaf.','Laumon’s derived base-change formula supplies the correctly typed statement.','The missing e_* is an editorial restoration, not a new ink reading.'),
    53:('Two signs conflict under a fixed translation convention.','ForT_t(b)=b+t, the kernel character is trivial atb=−t. Thus Φ(P_t) is supported at−t.','The modern translation formula resolves the mathematics once the convention is fixed.','The overwritten source sign remains a reading question.'),
    54:('A heuristic fractional-power expression.','Mukai Proposition3.11 was visually checked. General nondegenerate line bundles use an index and|χ|; the ample case has index0 andχ>0.','The ample pullback formula is established and yields the rational Chern character.','No literal fractional line bundle or unrestricted relative statement is asserted.'),
    55:('An unflagged coefficient error.','Symbolic expansion gives c2=(r−1)D′²/(2r), c3=−(r−1)(r−2)D′³/(6r²). The elliptic-product example has degree1, versus written degree2.','The displayed coefficients are false even modulo torsion.','Correct the algebra explicitly; the weaker final integrality statement can survive.'),
    57:('A weaker integral-cycle conclusion follows the faulty expansion.','The final coefficient is r(−1)^kck(E), an integral multiple of an actual Chern class in the ample field case.','Mukai’s bundle theorem makes this qualified salvage valid.','This is weaker than unrestricted integral Fourier duality.'),
    58:('An explicit torsion-sensitive question.','Separated integral lift, equality modulo torsion and Fourier identities. Beckmann–deGaayFortman Theorem3.8 and Question3.9 were read.','The full question remains open in general. The2025 theorem inverts(2g+d+1)! and imposes base/lifting assumptions; its sl2 refinement also inverts the polarization degree.','Do not report the recent denominator-controlled theorem as a full integral solution.'),
    59:('A GRR calculation.','Both projection and addition have the indicated pulled-back Todd factor. It is invertible in the rational smooth-base Chow setting.','The qualified rational Fourier identities are established.','An arbitrary singular base is outside the verified comparison.'),
    60:('An incomplete relative factor and ambiguous product symbol.','Both Todd factors and ch(ω_A) are needed before applying the Hodge-sequence cancellation.','Moonen corrects the Deninger–Murre bundle-duality slip and proves the qualified Todd cancellation; stronger Chern vanishing uses the stated extra comparison.','No arbitrary-base vanishing result is claimed.'),
    61:('Product-exchange formulas with an omitted convolution mark.','The parity sign follows from the derived shift; the two products are tracked with one Poincaré convention.','The field identities follow from established Fourier theory.','Keep relative Todd corrections separate.'),
    62:('An allegation that Kleiman omitted a sign.','The opened candidate2A12 only states Pontryagin-to-cup, where no parity sign is needed;2A13 uses another star convention.','The cited candidate does not verify the allegation. No exact erratum match was found.','Do not accept the manuscript annotation as an established correction to Kleiman.'),
    63:('An undefined check onF accompanies derived duality.','Grothendieck duality replaces P byP∨ and addsω_A[g]; P∨ is obtained by inversion on either abelian factor.','Mukai and Laumon establish the qualified formula.','One compatible check convention is proposed, without changing the diplomatic text.'),
    65:('The characteristic-zero identification is asserted.','The tangent extension has kernel t_B∨ and quotient t_A, matching H¹_dR(B). Coleman’s exact base hypotheses were read.','Universal-extension/deRham comparison is established. The opened proof allows a reduced base or a base flat overZ.','The source’s characteristic-zero case is covered; arbitrary-base scope is not inferred.'),
    66:('The degree-one compatibility is explicitly deferred.','A perfect degree-one pairing induces the exterior Hodge pairings. Matching dimensions alone does not construct that pairing.','Coleman Theorem1.1 compares the relevant constructions under its precise hypotheses.','The visible A/B differential-sheaf typo is an editorial issue.'),
    67:('A Cartier-duality diagram and orthogonality claim.','Duality exchangesF andV; each Frobenius kernel has orderp^g and is the annihilator of the other under the finite Cartier pairing.','Oda§1 verifies the finite-group-scheme comparison.','This concerns group schemes, not only geometric points.'),
    68:('A restricted-Lie extension, not merely vector spaces.','The p-operation is essential. SGA3VII_B Corollary4.4.1 supplies the height-one equivalence.','The structural comparison is established in the restricted category.','An ordinary vector-space extension does not determine the group scheme.'),
    69:('An explicit reconstruction question.','Oda Corollary5.11 was read on the scanned page: M(A[p]) identifies functorially with H¹_dR(A), andVM is the Hodge subspace.','Solved over a perfect field of characteristicp by Oda.','Do not extend the theorem to arbitrary bases or abstract p-torsion points.'),
    70:('Reused flattening proposition, cancelled freeness corollary and compressed margin.','Stacks051R verifies generic freeness. The opened05P7 is a definition, not an existence theorem for every flattening functor.','The generic-freeness part is established; exact publication matching of the full PropositionA was not completed.','Keep the fixed affine cover and all finite-presentation hypotheses.'),
    71:('A cancelled graded-category draft;TF is undefined.','Noetherian completion is exact. A finite graded module is detected by its lowest nonzero component; the ungraded modulek[x]/(x−1) completes tozero.','The qualified graded statement is standard; faithful flatness on all modules needs an additional Jacobson-radical condition.','The ungraded counterexample does not refute the actual graded assertion.'),
    72:('A programme with an explicitly unidentified equivalence relation.','Separated the quotient construction, universal regular property, complementary duality and positivity.','Modern algebraic representatives solve selected codimensions, especially2; they do not identify the author’s unknown relation in all degrees.','The2026 torsor refinement presupposes a regular homomorphism and does not solve general existence.'),
    73:('A uniform bound is proposed over all cycle families.','Kahn’s corrected boundedness argument and ACMV Proposition8.2 were checked; the latter coversi=1,2,dimX.','The codimension2 bound and existence theorem are established. The all-codimension quantifier is not proved by those references.','A bound on one chosen Abel–Jacobi image is insufficient for the source’s quantifier.'),
    74:('A subquotient is proposed first, an injection hoped for next.','ACMV8.2 requires smooth properX, a surjective regular map, a miniversal-cycle degree r, andℓ≠p withℓ∤r; target torsion is removed.','The precise integral injection is established in the specified codimensions.','Do not replace it by an all-prime or all-codimension assertion.'),
    75:('A later comparison testing an identification.','Ottem–Suzuki Corollary4.2 uses an Enriques threefold times an elliptic curve; the Walker factorization has a nontrivial isogeny kernel.','The Abel–Jacobi map need not be universal in codimension3.','This is not nonexistence of an algebraic representative, and does not refute an undefined J^i.'),
    76:('A conjectural pencil formula with an inserted fibre condition and uncertain sign.','The8August1964 letter confirms a surface-fibration comparison. Künnemann’s theorem concerns higher heights on abelian varieties over number fields.','These are meaningful partial comparators, not exact proofs of the underdefined general pencil display.','Fix the height normalization, vertical terms and cycle quotient before claiming a solution.'),
    77:('An explicit positivity gap.','The negative of an ample symmetric class is nondegenerate but not ample. This logical test does not satisfy every cycle-origin condition in the proposed theorem.','ACMV2025 constructs qualified symmetric isogenies; positivity in characteristicp still requires the lifting or other hypotheses in§13.','Keep symmetry, descent, isogeny and ampleness as separate assertions.'),
    78:('The symbolτ is undefined locally.','Under the algebraic-equivalence-up-to-multiple interpretation, Clemens’s nonzero rational Griffiths group yields higher-codimension counterexamples.','The divisor theorem is a different, valid special case. The all-codimension interpretation is false.','Do not confuseτ with homological equivalence or standard conjectureD.'),
    79:('Reused chamber-theory text; authorship is not established.','Local finiteness gives a ball meeting only one wall at a generic wall point. Its two half-balls determine adjacent chambers; continuation along the relative interior preserves them.','The elementary arrangement statement is valid.','No reflection or Coxeter structure follows from the stated hypotheses alone.'),
    80:('The source distinguishes associativity from nondegeneracy.','Associativity reduces to the four-linear alternating identity. The V2,W0 computation has defect1, showing why nondegeneracy alone is insufficient.','The formal criterion is verified; no exact later development of this particular model was located.','This is an algebra model, not a geometric realization theorem.'),
    81:('An isotropic-image example.','ForQ=diag(1,−1), the vectorξ+w has normzero, so the induced four-form vanishes;φ andQ remain nondegenerate.','The example is valid over the explicitly specified field and characteristic.','No geometric realization or uniqueness is claimed.'),
    82:('The source asks about orbit size and cyclic span, with a4-versus6 doubt.','A scalar eigenvalue that is not a root of unity gives an infinite orbit with one-dimensional span. The two requested properties are different.','No exact later development matching the normalization was found.','Fix the field and tensor convention before settling the stronger claim.'),
    83:('An earlier-run explicit reconstruction.','The dim6 computation gives detQ=2097152/59049, Q(ξ,ξ)=1 and cyclic determinant−32/27. A positive row-sum bound proves an infinite orbit for that normalization.','The witness was independently recomputed.','It proves existence, not minimality or geometric realization.'),
    84:('An earlier-run family, not a new author statement.','Exact casesm=1,…,4 were checked. The general argument uses a nonzero Vandermonde minor and avoids the finitely many degeneracy polynomials after rational perturbation.','The qualified construction gives unbounded cyclic rank within the specified algebra model.','The field, normalization and nonvanishing conditions remain explicit.'),
    86:('An unflagged false step on c16:53.','OnH*(P²),n=2,k=1,T1=diag(0,1,0);LT1(h)=h² and unit loweringu givesuLT1=π2≠π1. Inserting targetT1 kills this unwanted component.','The literal vanishing is refuted. The repaired formulaπ_k=u_kT_kL^(n−k)T_k proves the intended induction.','This is a new review correction, not a changed reading or a new open problem.')
    }
    for c in C:
        n=int(c['id'].rsplit('-',1)[1])-16000
        if n in wording:
            c['status_on_pages'],c['computation'],c['fate'],c['present_status']=wording[n]
        if n==107:c['class']='B'
    R['Deligne1980']['locator']='Théorème4.1.1, PDFp80 visually read; journal pagination not inferred from collected-volume running folios'
    R['Conrad2014']['locator']='Definition1.3.3 and reflection uniqueness pp27–28/PDFp26; Examples1.3.8–1.3.10; explicit integrality condition in root-system definition'
    return C
